# K03 S4 (the author, 2026-10-06; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption): in a value position too a
# resolved head is consumed by its own contract -- a word of the language, bare or applied to nothing, is its
# application with no argument, refused at the word, never an unresolved name or a conversion; a named
# Structure's name is a reference, and its Frame gives a structural value;
# neither is a numeric operand. The refusal is the ordinary kind mismatch.
Model:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Model
fn: take (int: v) int
    return: v
end: take
fn: m () int
    int: w 5
    w: Model() + 1
    return: w
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
